Subject: [PATCH 5/6] An opt-in hook: the port's safety fixtures, run on a worker by a hidden command
Upstream: memcached 1.6.45
Upstream-Archive: https://memcached.org/files/memcached-1.6.45.tar.gz
Upstream-SHA256: d362c64e6d8d5287153501eabf7c85b4a761432fbf53f5d7b085d0bb1653c1dd
Build-Variants: only with -DMC_CAPSTONE_SAFETY_FIXTURES (host/build-safety.sh); every other build is unchanged
Depends-On: none
Apply-From: upstream source root, with patch --batch --forward --fuzz=0 -p1

The port's Safety milestone asks what a heap overflow, a use after free and a stale free do in the
memcached domain, on each heap arm, with the fault in a worker as a real one would be. A build with
MC_CAPSTONE_SAFETY_FIXTURES includes ports/memcached/app/src/mcapp-safety.c into proto_text.c (the
build copies it beside the file) and answers `mc_capstone_fixture <n>` by running fixture n on the
worker that took the connection, which ends the process with the fixture's mark or faults. The
oracle's and the marker's images are built without it.

One fixture also reverses an upstream fix at run time: in slabs_mover.c, with mcapp_reverse_a836eab
set (fixture 22 only), an item that is allocated but not yet linked is taken for cleared, as before
a836eab, instead of MOVE_BUSY_FLOATING. Unset, the mover is upstream's.

--- a/proto_text.c
+++ b/proto_text.c
@@ -19,6 +19,12 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 
+#ifdef MC_CAPSTONE_SAFETY_FIXTURES
+/* the port's safety fixtures (ports/memcached/app/src/mcapp-safety.c), copied beside this file by
+   host/build-safety.sh: only that build defines MC_CAPSTONE_SAFETY_FIXTURES */
+#include "mcapp-safety.c"
+#endif
+
 #define _DO_CAS true
 #define _NO_CAS false
 #define _DO_TOUCH true
@@ -1536,6 +1542,11 @@
     }
 
     t->cur_sfd = c->sfd; // cuddle sfd for logging.
+#ifdef MC_CAPSTONE_SAFETY_FIXTURES
+    /* `mc_capstone_fixture <n>`: run fixture n on this worker; it never returns (exit(mark)) */
+    if (cmdlen > 20 && strncmp(command, "mc_capstone_fixture ", 20) == 0)
+        mcapp_run_fixture(atoi(command + 20));
+#endif
     int ret = process_request(&pr, command, cmdlen);
     c->resp->noreply = pr.noreply;
     if (settings.verbose > 1) {
--- a/slabs_mover.c
+++ b/slabs_mover.c
@@ -322,6 +322,15 @@
             /* See above comment. No ITEM_SLABBED or ITEM_LINKED. Mark
              * busy and wait for item to complete its upload. */
             status = MOVE_BUSY_FLOATING;
+#ifdef MC_CAPSTONE_SAFETY_FIXTURES
+            {
+                /* fixture 22 reverses a836eab: before it, this item fell through as MOVE_PASS
+                   and its page was cleared under its holder */
+                extern volatile int mcapp_reverse_a836eab;
+                if (mcapp_reverse_a836eab)
+                    status = MOVE_PASS;
+            }
+#endif
         }
     }
 
